<%# The invite link for a waiting online match, shown to the player who created it and to
    nobody else: the address of the match is public, the token is not, so a viewer who opens
    the match page must not be able to read it.

    The plain link is always there, as a link and as its own text, which is what a visitor
    with JavaScript switched off copies. The copy button is hidden until the Stimulus
    controller reveals it, so a page without JavaScript never shows a control that cannot do
    anything.

    link is nil in a broadcast (there is no host outside a request) and nil once the match has
    been joined or cancelled, which is exactly when the panel should disappear. The wrapper
    keeps its id either way so a broadcast can replace it. %>
<div id="<%= Match::INVITE_ID %>">
  <% if link.present? && match.waiting? && seats.any? %>
    <section class="invite" data-controller="clipboard" aria-labelledby="invite-heading">
      <h2 class="invite__heading" id="invite-heading">Invite a player</h2>
      <p class="invite__note">
        Send this link to the person you want to play. They sign in, open it, and take the
        <%= side_label(match.free_seat) %> seat.
      </p>

      <div class="invite__link">
        <label class="invite__label" for="invite-link">Invite link</label>
        <input class="invite__field" id="invite-link" type="text" readonly value="<%= link %>"
               data-clipboard-target="source" spellcheck="false">
        <button type="button" class="button button--quiet invite__copy" hidden
                data-clipboard-target="button" data-action="clipboard#copy">Copy link</button>
      </div>
      <p class="invite__status" role="status" data-clipboard-target="status"></p>
      <p class="invite__plain">Or send the address itself: <%= link_to link, link, class: "invite__address" %></p>

      <div class="button-row">
        <%= button_to "Cancel this match", match_cancellation_path(match),
              class: "button button--quiet" %>
      </div>
    </section>
  <% end %>
</div>
